          "kind": "table",
          "title": "From the past to the future",
          "columns": [
            "Tense",
            "Use it for",
            "How it is made",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Perfect",
              "one finished action in the past",
              "*avoir* or *être* in the present, plus a past participle",
              "*hier, j'ai joué au foot*: yesterday I played football"
            ],
            [
              "Imperfect",
              "what used to happen, what was going on, and descriptions in the past",
              "the *nous* form without *-ons*, plus *-ais, -ais, -ait, -ions, -iez, -aient*",
              "*quand j'étais petit, je jouais au parc*: when I was little I used to play in the park"
            ],
            [
              "Present",
              "now, and what usually happens",
              "the stem plus the present endings",
              "*maintenant, je joue au tennis*: now I play tennis"
            ],
            [
              "Near future",
              "what is going to happen",
              "*aller* in the present, plus an infinitive",
              "*ce soir, je vais jouer*: this evening I am going to play"
            ],
            [
              "Future (Higher)",
              "what will happen",
              "the infinitive, *-re* verbs dropping the *e*, plus *-ai, -as, -a, -ons, -ez, -ont*",
              "*l'année prochaine, je jouerai*: next year I will play"
            ],
            [
              "Conditional",
              "what would happen",
              "the future stem plus the imperfect endings",
              "*je voudrais jouer*: I would like to play"
            ]
          ],
          "note": "At Foundation tier the conditional is only *je voudrais*, *tu voudrais*, *il voudrait*: would like. The imperative gives orders: *tourne à gauche*, turn left."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "body": "**Aim for three tenses in every longer answer.** A past, a present and a future, each signalled by a time phrase, is what lifts a piece of writing or speaking into the higher mark bands."
        }
      ],
      "applications": [
        {
          "title": "A speaking answer that scores",
          "body": "Asked about holidays: *l'année dernière je suis allé en Espagne* (past), *d'habitude je reste en France* (present), *l'année prochaine je vais visiter l'Italie* (future). Three tenses in three sentences."
